  "question": "Let $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ be two non-zero vectors such that $|\\vec{a}| = 4$, $|\\vec{b}| = 7$, and the projection of $\\vec{a}$ on $\\vec{b}$ plus the projection of $\\vec{b}$ on $\\vec{a}$ equals $5$. If $\\theta$ is the angle between $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$, find $\\theta$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Let $\\text{proj}_{\\vec{b}} \\vec{a} = \\dfrac{\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}}{|\\vec{b}|}$ and $\\text{proj}_{\\vec{a}} \\vec{b} = \\dfrac{\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}}{|\\vec{a}|}$.<br /><br />Given:<br /><br />$\\dfrac{\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}}{|\\vec{b}|} + \\dfrac{\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}}{|\\vec{a}|} = 5$<br /><br />Let $x = \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}$.<br /><br />$\\dfrac{x}{7} + \\dfrac{x}{4} = 5$<br /><br />$x\\left(\\dfrac{1}{7} + \\dfrac{1}{4}\\right) = 5$<br /><br />$\\dfrac{1}{7} + \\dfrac{1}{4} = \\dfrac{11}{28}$<br /><br />$x \\cdot \\dfrac{11}{28} = 5$<br /><br />$x = \\dfrac{140}{11}$<br /><br />Now,<br /><br />$x = |\\vec{a}| |\\vec{b}| \\cos \\theta$<br /><br />$\\dfrac{140}{11} = 4 \\times 7 \\cos \\theta$<br /><br />$28 \\cos \\theta = \\dfrac{140}{11}$<br /><br />$\\cos \\theta = \\dfrac{140}{308} = \\dfrac{35}{77}$<br /><br />Thus,<br /><br />$\\theta = \\cos^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{35}{77}\\right)$.",
